0011-cache-empty-glyphs-and-font-names.patch

Stop asking CoreText about blank cells on every row rebuild.

MetalTerminalRenderer.glyphEntry(for:glyph:) cached only SUCCESSFUL rasterizations.
CoreTextGlyphRasterizer.rasterize(font:glyph:) returns nil for a zero-bounds glyph
(CoreTextGlyphRasterizer.swift:10-13), and the space glyph has zero bounds, so every
blank cell of every rebuilt row called CTFontGetBoundingRectsForGlyphs again. A pane
whose only activity is an agent spinner rebuilds its row ~12 times a second, and a
3s `sample` of such a pane put 23 of 37 row-build stacks in that call. The cache key
also called CTFontCopyPostScriptName per glyph, which showed in the same sample.

Two changes, both in Apple/Metal/MetalTerminalRenderer.swift:

1. emptyGlyphs: Set<GlyphKey> remembers a rasterizer miss, so a blank glyph reaches
   CoreText once per (font, size, glyph) instead of once per cell per rebuild. It is
   cleared with glyphCache on an atlas reset. Atlas-full nils are NOT cached; they
   are retried after the reset exactly as before.

2. postScriptName(of:) memoizes the key's font name by CTFont identity (the font is
   held strongly, so the identifier cannot be reused). Both glyphEntry call sites
   pass a scaledFontFor result, so it holds one entry per scaledFontCache entry.

No change to what is drawn: a nil entry was already skipped by both callers.

Gate: app/Scripts/check-metal-renderer.sh and check-metal-throughput.sh (no
regression); the CPU effect is measured, not gated (see the PR).

--- a/Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/Metal/MetalTerminalRenderer.swift
+++ b/Sources/SwiftTerm/Apple/Metal/MetalTerminalRenderer.swift
@@ -199,6 +199,17 @@
     private let colorAtlas: GlyphAtlas
     private let rasterizer = CoreTextGlyphRasterizer()
     private var glyphCache: [GlyphKey: GlyphEntry] = [:]
+    // Glyphs the rasterizer declined (zero bounds: the SPACE glyph, and any other
+    // blank). glyphCache only ever held successes, so every blank cell of every rebuilt
+    // row went back to CTFontGetBoundingRectsForGlyphs — the dominant cost of an
+    // otherwise idle pane whose only activity is an agent spinner repainting its row.
+    private var emptyGlyphs: Set<GlyphKey> = []
+    // PostScript name per scaled font, so glyphEntry builds its key without calling
+    // CTFontCopyPostScriptName (a CF copy + bridge) once per glyph. Keyed by identity;
+    // the font is held strongly so an ObjectIdentifier can never be reused for a
+    // different font. Both glyphEntry call sites pass a scaledFontFor result, so this
+    // holds exactly one entry per scaledFontCache entry and grows no faster than it.
+    private var fontNameCache: [ObjectIdentifier: (font: CTFont, name: String)] = [:]
     private var scaledFontCache: [GlyphKey: CTFont] = [:]
     private var customGlyphCache: [CustomGlyphKey: CustomGlyphEntry] = [:]
     private let imageTextureCache = NSMapTable<AnyObject, MTLTexture>(keyOptions: .weakMemory, valueOptions: .strongMemory)
@@ -1464,6 +1475,7 @@
     private func handleAtlasChange(_ atlas: GlyphAtlas, previousSize: Int) {
         if atlas.didReset {
             glyphCache.removeAll()
+            emptyGlyphs.removeAll()
             customGlyphCache.removeAll()
             rowCache.removeAll()
             atlasInvalidatedDuringBuild = true
@@ -1473,14 +1485,33 @@
         }
     }
 
+    private func postScriptName(of font: CTFont) -> String {
+        let id = ObjectIdentifier(font)
+        if let cached = fontNameCache[id] {
+            return cached.name
+        }
+        let name = CTFontCopyPostScriptName(font) as String
+        fontNameCache[id] = (font, name)
+        return name
+    }
+
     private func glyphEntry(for font: CTFont, glyph: CGGlyph) -> GlyphEntry? {
-        let key = GlyphKey(fontName: CTFontCopyPostScriptName(font) as String,
+        let key = GlyphKey(fontName: postScriptName(of: font),
                            size: CTFontGetSize(font),
                            glyph: glyph)
         if let cached = glyphCache[key] {
             return cached
+        }
+        if emptyGlyphs.contains(key) {
+            return nil
         }
         guard let bitmap = rasterizer.rasterize(font: font, glyph: glyph) else {
+            // Remember the miss: the answer depends only on (font, size, glyph), so asking
+            // CoreText again per blank cell per row rebuild is pure waste. An atlas reset
+            // clears this set with glyphCache, which also bounds a (never observed)
+            // transient CGContext failure in the rasterizer to one atlas generation.
+            // Atlas-full nils below are NOT cached: they are retried after the reset.
+            emptyGlyphs.insert(key)
             return nil
         }
         let atlasKind: GlyphAtlasKind = bitmap.isColor ? .color : .grayscale
